    "text": "This solution is a safe baseline and does not move the sleigh. It loads and delivers every gift whose recipient is already within distance D of (0, 0), so no carrots or acceleration are needed.\n\nDistances are compared as integers (c\u00b2 + r\u00b2 \u2264 D\u00b2), which avoids floating-point error. Each qualifying gift produces a `LoadGift` and a `DeliverGift` action, so the action count is twice the number of such gifts. This is valid because loading and delivery both happen at time 0 with the sleigh at the origin, and no `Float` is issued. Gifts farther than D from the origin are not delivered. I did not implement movement to reach them, so this scores only the gifts near Lapland and is likely well below what a routing approach would get.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main(){\n    long long T,D,W,G;\n    cin>>T>>D>>W>>G;\n    for(int i=0;i<W;i++){long long a,b;cin>>a>>b;}\n    vector<string> out;\n    for(int i=0;i<G;i++){\n        string n;long long s,w,c,r;\n        cin>>n>>s>>w>>c>>r;\n        if(c*c+r*r<=D*D){\n            out.push_back(\"LoadGift \"+n);\n            out.push_back(\"DeliverGift \"+n);\n        }\n    }\n    printf(\"%d\\n\",(int)out.size());\n    for(auto&s:out)printf(\"%s\\n\",s.c_str());\n}\n```",
    "type": "text"
   }
